TOOL_RESULT retrieve_history:
{"results": [], "n_results": 0}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{"action":"final","output":{
  "research_concepts":[
    "opponent next-possession PPP",
    "play-type labeling",
    "AVOID labels",
    "own-sequence lags",
    "NBA play-by-play data",
    "possession-level PPP",
    "data quality"
  ],
  "methodological_questions":[
    "How is opponent next-possession PPP defined and measured?",
    "What threshold of PPP justifies labeling a play as AVOID?",
    "Do own-sequence lags influence the PPP after a play?",
    "What are appropriate controls to isolate the effect of labeling?",
    "How to handle confounding by game context and opponent strength?",
    "Is the sample size for specific play types sufficient?"
  ],
  "historical_evidence":[
  ],
  "failed_approaches":[
  ],
  "evidence_establishes":[
    "None"
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish":[
    "None"
  ],
  "own_inferences":[
    "The question can be translated into an observational comparison of opponent PPP following plays that would be labeled AVOID versus those that would not, conditional on the same set of covariates.",
    "Because labeling is deterministic given the PPP threshold, the causal interpretation hinges on controlling for all factors that jointly influence PPP and play selection."
  ],
  "uncertainties":[
    "Exact PPP computation algorithm and its reliability across seasons.",
    "The true threshold that would optimally separate play types for AVOID labeling.",
    "The frequency of rare play types that may limit statistical power."
  ],
  "historical_effect":{
    "changed_decision":"no_historical_evidence",
    "explanation":"No prior studies were retrieved, so the decision is based entirely on the data and methodological considerations above."
  },
  "testability":{
    "p_testable":0.75,
    "blocking_constraints":[
      {
        "code":"EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
        "text":"Some play types of interest may occur infrequently, limiting power for those specific comparisons."
      },
      {
        "code":"CONFOUNDING",
        "text":"Opponent PPP is influenced by many contextual factors; residual confounding may bias estimates."
      }
    ]
  },
  "prior_work":{
    "already_answered":"unknown",
    "cited":[
    ],
    "summary":"No relevant prior work was found in the retrieval step."
  },
  "risks":[
    {
      "code":"EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
      "text":"Rare play types may not provide enough observations for robust estimates."
    },
    {
      "code":"CONFOUNDING",
      "text":"Unobserved game context variables could jointly affect play selection and opponent PPP."
    },
    {
      "code":"MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
      "text":"PPP calculations rely on accurate play‑by‑play parsing; any systematic error could bias results."
    },
    {
      "code":"MULTIPLE_TESTING",
      "text":"Testing many thresholds or play types increases the chance of false positives if not pre‑registered."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome":{
    "supported":0.4,
    "rejected":0.2,
    "untestable":0.1,
    "artifact":0.2,
    "uncertain":0.1
  },
  "decision":"proceed_with_changes",
  "design":{
    "estimand":"Difference in opponent next‑possession PPP between possessions that would be labeled AVOID (PPP>threshold) and those that would not, conditioned on covariates.",
    "unit":"possession",
    "sample":"All recorded possessions from NBA 2022‑23 through 2025‑26 seasons (regular season and playoffs) where play‑type and PPP can be computed.",
    "power":"With the full dataset (~8–10 million possessions) we expect >0.90 power to detect a 0.5‑point PPP difference (≈1.5% of average PPP). For rare play types power will be evaluated separately.",
    "controls":"Opponent team fixed effects, game location, period, score differential, current points differential, and time remaining. Optional match‑by‑match fixed effects to absorb game‑specific unobservables.",
    "falsification":"Apply the same analysis to a random labeling threshold (e.g., 50th percentile PPP) and to play types that are theoretically unrelated to opponent PPP to check for spurious associations.",
    "multiplicity":"Pre‑register a single primary hypothesis (threshold 60th percentile PPP) and one secondary hypothesis (threshold 70th percentile). Use Bonferroni correction for these two tests.",
    "decision_rule":"Reject the null of no association if p<0.025 after correction; otherwise report the estimate and 95% CI.",
    "data_version":"Latest available NBA stats API data up to 2026‑06‑19, including all play‑by‑play, substitution, and possession records."
  }
}}

